==Malay==

===Etymology===
{{clipping|ms|empunya}}, from {{inh|ms|poz-pro|*əmpuña}}, from {{inh|ms|poz-pro|*əmpu}}. Compare {{cog|tl|impó|t=grandmother}}.<ref>{{R:map:ACD|empu}}</ref>

First attested in the {{w|Talang Tuo inscription}}, 684 AD, as {{m+|ms-old||tr=punyā}} in the form {{m|ms-old||tr=punyāña}}.

In the sense of possessive/genitive particle, {{sl|ms|nan-hbl|-|nocap=1}} {{zh-l|的|tr=ê}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|ms|/puɲa/}}
** {{IPA|ms|[pu.ɲə]|a=Johor-Riau}}
*** {{audio|ms|LL-Q9237 (msa)-GinormousBuildings-punya (JR).wav|a=Malaysia}}
** {{IPA|ms|[pu.ɲa]|a=Baku}}
*** {{audio|ms|LL-Q9237 (msa)-GinormousBuildings-punya (B).wav|a=Malaysia}}
* {{rhymes|ms|ɲa|a|s2=2}}
* {{hyph|ms|pu|nya}}

===Noun===
{{ms-noun|j=ڤوڽا|pl=-|ku=-|nya=-|mu=-}}

# Someone who [[own]]s a [[certain]] thing; an [[owner]].
#: {{syn|ms|pemunya|pemilik|empunya|tuan|yang punya|tuan punya}}
# Something that is [[own]]ed; a [[possession]].
#: {{syn|ms|kepunyaan|hak|milik}}
#: {{uxi|ms|rumah '''punya''' Adam|house that is Adam's '''possession'''}}

===Particle===
{{head|ms|particle|Jawi spelling|ڤوڽا|alternative form|nya}}

# {{lb|ms|informal}} {{n-g|Used to indicate possession, similar to English [['s]].}}
#: {{uxi|ms|Adam '''punya''' buku|Adam''''s''' book}}

====Usage notes====
* The more formal way to indicate possession in Malay is by placing the possessed object in front of the possessor, so that, to say "Adam's book", instead of saying "''Adam punya buku''", one just says "''buku Adam''".

===Verb===
{{ms-verb|j=ڤوڽا}}

# To [[have]].
#: {{syn|ms|punyai|ada}}
#: {{ux|ms|Saya '''punya''' enam buku.|I '''have''' six books.}}
# To [[own]].
#: {{syn|ms|punyai}}
#: {{ux|ms|Saya '''punya''' dua buah rumah.|I '''own''' two houses.}}
# {{lb|ms|spoken}} {{n-g|Emphasizes a word that is repeated.}}

